# playpick cell: mode=clear spec=paladin:retribution style=wander size=25
# difficulty=heroic view=390x844,touch save=fresh.
#
# A fresh profile locks 25-heroic, so #b=marrow&s=25&h=1 unlocks the tier the
# same way every other 25-heroic clear/walk script in this ledger does since
# the 2026-09-26 driver-lesson, then backs out to a real RAID -> WALK IN at
# the door rather than the invite's single-fight "visiting" framing.
#
# Checked sessions.jsonl first: this exact spec/style/size/difficulty cell
# was already run once, on 2026-09-24 (plans/2026-09-25-4.play), before that
# recipe existed -- it never actually reached heroic at all, because the
# script walked in from the raid-setup screen's own locked default (10N) and
# the ledger line says so outright ("25-heroic is locked on a fresh save so
# the walk ran on the setup screen default"). So every reading that session
# produced -- the vigil wipe, the stuck PULL AGAIN -- is a 10-normal reading
# wearing a 25-heroic label. This is the first time paladin:retribution under
# wander is actually walked through the citadel at real 25-heroic, and the
# first time this exact cell runs on a portrait phone viewport (the 2026-09-24
# attempt was 844x390 landscape; every other 390x844-touch clear-mode session
# on record used a different spec or style).
#
# direction.md's #6 (vigil stalls any evening near y=-1560..-1573 regardless
# of style) and #3 (a travel-mode wipe's PULL AGAIN never revives the party)
# are both already confirmed across six-plus specs/styles/saves/viewports, so
# this cell's main news value is the real-vs-fallback-difficulty distinction
# above -- but watching for either shape anyway, since no paladin has yet run
# wander through a genuine heroic vigil.
open #b=marrow&s=25&h=1
tap back
tap raid
shot raid-setup
tap next
tap class:paladin:retribution
shot class-selected
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state
shot start
targets
ui
evening wander 200 6
shot end
state
says
bill
